### =====================================================================
### ALMACÉN BIM — pruebas completas de la API (REST Client de VS Code)
### =====================================================================
# Cómo usarlo
#  1. Backend corriendo (npm run dev). Ajustar baseUrl / credenciales si hace falta.
#  2. Ejecutar de arriba hacia abajo: cada bloque captura los ids que necesita
#     el siguiente (# @name + {{nombre.response.body.$.campo}}).
#  3. La sección 0 crea un proyecto NUEVO cada vez. Para reutilizar uno, dejar
#     `@projectId` fijo (descomentar la línea de abajo) y omitir el bloque 0.2.
#  4. La sección 12 (bajas y vaciar Almacén) es DESTRUCTIVA: borra datos.
#  5. Los archivos de ejemplo están en ./ejemplos (PDF y modelo .gltf mínimos).
#
# Permisos (módulo almacen): ver = view; crear/editar/adjuntar = process;
# bajas de estructura/catálogo = delete; bajas de documentos de auditoría
# (proveedor, requerimiento) y vaciar = configure / dueño o admin del proyecto.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
# @projectId = 1

### =====================================================================
### 0. SESIÓN Y PROYECTO
### =====================================================================

### 0.1 Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ismael@email.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

###
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 0.2 Crear un proyecto de prueba (todos los campos son obligatorios, aunque sean null)
# @name project
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Prueba Almacén (.http)",
  "description": null,
  "location": null,
  "client": null,
  "contractor": null,
  "start_date": "2026-09-01",
  "end_date": null
}

###
@projectId = {{project.response.body.$.project_id}}

### =====================================================================
### 1. CATÁLOGOS
### =====================================================================

### 1.1 Estilos de almacén (catálogo global, sin proyecto)
# @name styles
GET {{baseUrl}}/warehouse-styles
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
@styleId = {{styles.response.body.$[0].warehouse_style_id}}

### 1.2 Categorías del proyecto: Partida (fija), Materiales y Equipo (relacionales).
# Se crean solas con el proyecto; no hay endpoints para crearlas ni borrarlas.
# @name categories
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
# Revisar el orden en la respuesta y ajustar los índices si hace falta.
@categoryPartidaId = {{categories.response.body.$[0].category_id}}
@categoryMaterialesId = {{categories.response.body.$[1].category_id}}

### =====================================================================
### 2. UBICACIONES: almacén → estante → casilla
### =====================================================================
# Las medidas van en metros; 1 cubo = 1.3 m. El almacén es una grilla de
# cubos; los estantes ocupan 1 o 2 cubos de profundidad.

### 2.1 Crear almacén (13 x 13 m = grilla de 10 x 10 cubos)
# @name warehouse
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Almacén central",
  "warehouse_style_id": {{styleId}},
  "corner1_x": 0, "corner1_z": 0,
  "corner2_x": 13, "corner2_z": 13,
  "direction": "norte",
  "grid_width": 10,
  "grid_depth": 10
}

###
@warehouseId = {{warehouse.response.body.$.warehouse_id}}

### 2.2 Listar / obtener almacenes
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses/{{warehouseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2.3 Editar almacén (PUT: se envían todos los campos)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses/{{warehouseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Almacén central (editado)",
  "warehouse_style_id": {{styleId}},
  "corner1_x": 0, "corner1_z": 0,
  "corner2_x": 13, "corner2_z": 13,
  "direction": "norte",
  "grid_width": 10,
  "grid_depth": 10
}

### 2.4 Crear estante: 2 cubos de ancho x 1 de fondo, 2 niveles. Genera sus casillas solo.
# direction: 0 o 1 (hacia dónde mira el estante)
# @name rack
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses/{{warehouseId}}/racks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Estante A",
  "corner1_x": 0, "corner1_z": 0,
  "corner2_x": 2.6, "corner2_z": 1.3,
  "levels": 2,
  "direction": 0
}

###
@rackId = {{rack.response.body.$.rack_id}}
@binId = {{rack.response.body.$.bins[0].bin_id}}
@binId2 = {{rack.response.body.$.bins[1].bin_id}}

### 2.5 Listar / obtener estantes (el detalle trae sus casillas con contenido)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses/{{warehouseId}}/racks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses/{{warehouseId}}/racks/{{rackId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2.6 Renombrar estante (PUT: solo el nombre)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses/{{warehouseId}}/racks/{{rackId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Estante A (editado)" }

### 2.7 Renombrar casilla (PATCH: solo el nombre; la casilla no se crea ni se borra sola)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses/{{warehouseId}}/racks/{{rackId}}/bins/{{binId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "A1 - herramientas" }

### 2.8 Buscar una ubicación por texto (nombre de almacén, estante o casilla)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/locations/search?q=herramientas
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =====================================================================
### 3. MODELOS 3D (biblioteca del USUARIO, reutilizable entre proyectos)
### =====================================================================

### 3.1 Subir un modelo (.glb o .gltf) — no cuelga de un proyecto
# @name asset
POST {{baseUrl}}/model-3d-assets
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Almacen

------Almacen
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="cubo.gltf"
Content-Type: model/gltf+json

< ./ejemplos/cubo.gltf
------Almacen--

###
@assetId = {{asset.response.body.$.model_3d_asset_id}}

### 3.2 Modelos disponibles en el proyecto (propios, del sistema o ya usados aquí)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/model-3d-assets
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 3.3 Contenido de un modelo
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/model-3d-assets/{{assetId}}/content
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =====================================================================
### 4. PRODUCTOS
### =====================================================================
# Categoría fija (Partida): se envía `code`. Relacional (Materiales/Equipo):
# se envía `base_product_code` (código de una partida existente); el código
# final es prefijo-código. La unidad se guarda en minúsculas.

### 4.1 Producto de categoría fija (Partida)
# @name product
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category_id": {{categoryPartidaId}},
  "code": "01.01.01",
  "name": "Cemento Portland tipo I",
  "unit": "bls"
}

###
@productId = {{product.response.body.$.product_id}}

### 4.2 Producto relacional (Materiales) basado en la partida anterior
# @name productMaterial
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category_id": {{categoryMaterialesId}},
  "base_product_code": "01.01.01",
  "name": "Cemento Sol (bolsa 42.5 kg)",
  "unit": "bls"
}

###
@productMaterialId = {{productMaterial.response.body.$.product_id}}

### 4.3 Listar (con filtro opcional por categoría) / obtener
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/products?category_id={{categoryPartidaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.4 Editar producto (PUT: nombre y unidad)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cemento Portland tipo I (editado)",
  "unit": "bls"
}

### 4.5 Asignar un modelo 3D al producto (null lo quita)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/products/{{productId}}/model-3d
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "model_3d_asset_id": {{assetId}} }

### =====================================================================
### 5. PROVEEDORES (por proyecto; el RUC es único entre los activos)
### =====================================================================

### 5.1 Crear proveedor (el RUC tolera espacios o guiones al escribirlo)
# @name supplier
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ruc": "20-123456789",
  "name": "Cementos del Sur S.A.C."
}

###
@supplierId = {{supplier.response.body.$.supplier_id}}

### 5.2 Listar y buscar (autocompletado): por el comienzo del RUC o por parte del nombre
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers?search=2012
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers?search=cementos
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5.3 Obtener uno (documents_count = cuántos documentos lo usan)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers/{{supplierId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5.4 Editar (PUT completo). El RUC solo cambia mientras no tenga documentos.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers/{{supplierId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ruc": "20123456789",
  "name": "Cementos del Sur SAC"
}

### =====================================================================
### 6. REQUERIMIENTOS (auditoría: no mueven stock)
### =====================================================================

### 6.1 Crear (con sus líneas; cada línea lleva un producto REAL del catálogo: si aún no existe,
# se crea antes con POST /products — el frontend lo ofrece dentro de la misma pantalla)
# @name requisition
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "number": "REQ-001",
  "requisition_date": "2026-09-10",
  "requester": "Almacenero de obra",
  "notes": "Para el vaciado de la losa",
  "items": [
    { "product_id": {{productId}}, "description": "Cemento Portland tipo I", "quantity_requested": 100, "estimated_unit_price": 28.5 },
    { "product_id": {{productMaterialId}}, "description": "Cemento Sol bolsa 42.5 kg (como dice el papel)", "quantity_requested": 20 }
  ]
}

###
@requisitionId = {{requisition.response.body.$.purchase_requisition_id}}
@requisitionItemId = {{requisition.response.body.$.items[0].purchase_requisition_item_id}}

### 6.2 Listar (con búsqueda opcional por número o solicitante) / obtener
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions?search=REQ
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions/{{requisitionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6.3 Editar la cabecera (PATCH parcial: solo lo enviado; notes null la limpia)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions/{{requisitionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requester": "Ing. Residente" }

### 6.4 Líneas: agregar / editar parcial / quitar (la última no se puede quitar)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions/{{requisitionId}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "product_id": {{productId}}, "description": "Alambre N°16", "quantity_requested": 5 }

###
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions/{{requisitionId}}/items/{{requisitionItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity_requested": 120, "estimated_unit_price": null }

###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions/{{requisitionId}}/items/{{requisitionItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6.5 Documento físico: (1) subir el archivo a `files` con module_code=almacen
# @name scan
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/files
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Almacen

------Almacen
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="module_code"

almacen
------Almacen
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="requerimiento-001.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./ejemplos/documento.pdf
------Almacen--

###
@scanId = {{scan.response.body.$.file_id}}

### 6.6 (2) adjuntarlo al requerimiento. Con file_id null se quita; reemplazar o quitar
# ELIMINA el archivo anterior del sistema (sin historial de versiones).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions/{{requisitionId}}/file
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "file_id": {{scanId}} }

### 6.7 Un archivo adjunto no se puede borrar desde /files (responde 409 FILE_IN_USE)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/files/{{scanId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6.8 Archivos del módulo (para ver el archivo pendiente/adjunto)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/files?module_code=almacen
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =====================================================================
### 7. INGRESOS (goods receipts) — suman stock; no se editan ni se borran
### =====================================================================
# La cantidad recibida (total_quantity) se reparte entre casillas (locations)
# y la suma tiene que dar EXACTO el total. quantity_per_delivery_note es lo
# que decía la guía (opcional).
# Guía de remisión: serie (1-4 letras/números, se pasa a mayúsculas) + número (1-8 dígitos).

### 7.1 Crear ingreso
# @name receipt
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/goods-receipts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "supplier_id": {{supplierId}},
  "delivery_note_series": "t001",
  "delivery_note_number": "123",
  "delivery_note_date": "2026-09-10",
  "received_date": "2026-09-12",
  "items": [
    {
      "product_id": {{productId}},
      "total_quantity": 97,
      "quantity_per_delivery_note": 100,
      "locations": [
        { "bin_id": {{binId}}, "quantity": 60 },
        { "bin_id": {{binId2}}, "quantity": 37 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

###
@receiptId = {{receipt.response.body.$.goods_receipt_id}}

### 7.2 Listar / obtener
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/goods-receipts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/goods-receipts/{{receiptId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =====================================================================
### 8. VALES DE SALIDA (goods issues) — restan stock
### =====================================================================

### 8.1 Crear vale (recipient_dni: 8 dígitos)
# @name issue
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/goods-issues
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_sector": "Sector 1",
  "destination_level": "Nivel 2",
  "destination_block": "Bloque A",
  "recipient_name": "Juan Pérez",
  "recipient_dni": "12345678",
  "issue_date": "2026-09-15",
  "items": [
    {
      "product_id": {{productId}},
      "total_quantity": 20,
      "locations": [ { "bin_id": {{binId}}, "quantity": 20 } ]
    }
  ]
}

###
@issueId = {{issue.response.body.$.goods_issue_id}}

### 8.2 Listar / obtener
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/goods-issues
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/goods-issues/{{issueId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =====================================================================
### 9. KARDEX (movimientos de inventario)
### =====================================================================

### 9.1 Todos los movimientos
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/inventory-movements
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 9.2 Filtrados por producto y rango de fechas (from/to opcionales)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/inventory-movements?product_id={{productId}}&from=2026-09-01&to=2026-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 9.3 Stock del producto y ubicación principal
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =====================================================================
### 10. RESUMEN DEL CONTENIDO DE ALMACÉN
### =====================================================================

### 10.1 Cuánto guarda Almacén en este proyecto (incluye lo dado de baja); is_empty
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/almacen/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =====================================================================
### 11. CASOS QUE DEBEN FALLAR (revisar el código de error)
### =====================================================================

### 11.1 RUC inválido → 400 INVALID_REQUEST_DATA
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ruc": "123", "name": "Proveedor con RUC malo" }

### 11.2 RUC repetido → 409 SUPPLIER_DUPLICATE_RUC
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ruc": "20123456789", "name": "Otro con el mismo RUC" }

### 11.3 Cambiar el RUC de un proveedor con documentos → 409 SUPPLIER_RUC_LOCKED
PUT {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers/{{supplierId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ruc": "20999999999", "name": "Cementos del Sur SAC" }

### 11.4 Baja de un proveedor con documentos → 409 SUPPLIER_HAS_DOCUMENTS
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/suppliers/{{supplierId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 11.5 Ingreso con la suma de casillas distinta al total → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/goods-receipts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "supplier_id": {{supplierId}},
  "delivery_note_series": "T001",
  "delivery_note_number": "124",
  "delivery_note_date": "2026-09-10",
  "items": [ { "product_id": {{productId}}, "total_quantity": 10, "locations": [ { "bin_id": {{binId}}, "quantity": 4 } ] } ]
}

### 11.6 Guía con formato libre (no es serie + número) → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/goods-receipts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "supplier_id": {{supplierId}},
  "delivery_note_series": "GR-23144141",
  "delivery_note_number": "abc",
  "delivery_note_date": "2026-09-10",
  "items": [ { "product_id": {{productId}}, "total_quantity": 10, "locations": [ { "bin_id": {{binId}}, "quantity": 10 } ] } ]
}

### 11.7 Vale por más stock del que hay → error de stock insuficiente
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/goods-issues
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destination_sector": "Sector 1", "destination_level": "Nivel 2", "destination_block": "Bloque A",
  "recipient_name": "Juan Pérez", "recipient_dni": "12345678", "issue_date": "2026-09-15",
  "items": [ { "product_id": {{productId}}, "total_quantity": 9999, "locations": [ { "bin_id": {{binId}}, "quantity": 9999 } ] } ]
}

### 11.8 Requerimiento sin líneas → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": "REQ-VACIO", "requisition_date": "2026-09-10", "requester": "Alguien", "items": [] }

### 11.9 Número de requerimiento repetido → 409 PURCHASE_REQUISITION_DUPLICATE_NUMBER
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": "REQ-001", "requisition_date": "2026-09-10", "requester": "Alguien", "items": [ { "product_id": {{productId}}, "description": "Algo", "quantity_requested": 1 } ] }

### 11.9b Línea sin producto → 400 (el producto del catálogo es obligatorio)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": "REQ-SIN-PRODUCTO", "requisition_date": "2026-09-10", "requester": "Alguien", "items": [ { "description": "Clavos sin catálogo", "quantity_requested": 1 } ] }

### 11.10 PATCH vacío → 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions/{{requisitionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 11.11 Eliminar un proyecto con Almacén con contenido → 409 ALMACEN_CONTENT_NOT_EMPTY
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =====================================================================
### 12. BAJAS Y VACIAR ALMACÉN  (DESTRUCTIVO)
### =====================================================================

### 12.1 Baja del requerimiento (exige configure; elimina también su archivo)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/purchase-requisitions/{{requisitionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 12.2 Baja de un producto sin movimientos (el que tiene historial se rechaza)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/products/{{productMaterialId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 12.3 Baja de un estante: se rechaza mientras tenga casillas (409 RACK_HAS_BINS)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/warehouses/{{warehouseId}}/racks/{{rackId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 12.4 VACIAR TODO ALMACÉN del proyecto (solo dueño/administrador). Conserva las 3 categorías.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/almacen/content
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 12.5 Ahora sí se puede eliminar el proyecto (si no hay contenido de otros módulos)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
